{
 "brief": "Palestinian education in the occupied West Bank faces systematic pressure through repeated demolition orders and partial school removals, Shehab Wire reported. Each new notice to demolish or remove sections of school buildings reduces the physical space available to students, particularly in Palestinian communities scattered across the territory.\n\nThe pattern of targeting schools does not appear to reflect isolated incidents but rather a coordinated approach that steadily constrains educational access. Officials and educators say the removals force children to travel greater distances or abandon schooling altogether, deepening the educational crisis in areas already struggling with limited resources and infrastructure.",
